    {
      "author_id": "615818451",
      "created_at": "2021-11-28T18:57:16.000Z",
      "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
        "1465032058254729216"
      ],
      "id": "1465032058254729216",
      "public_metrics": {
        "bookmark_count": 45,
        "impression_count": 0,
        "like_count": 271,
        "quote_count": 1,
        "reply_count": 6,
        "retweet_count": 28
      },
      "text": "Sunday is a day for building—great day to remember the great Steve Jobs quote:\n\n“Everything around you that you call 'life' was made up by people who were no smarter than you.\n\nAnd you can change it, you can influence it, you can build your own things that other people can use.”",
      "url": "https://x.com/alexandr_wang/status/1465032058254729216"
    },
    {
      "author_id": "615818451",
      "created_at": "2021-11-27T20:07:29.000Z",
      "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
        "1464687343198105601"
      ],
      "id": "1464687343198105601",
      "public_metrics": {
        "bookmark_count": 182,
        "impression_count": 0,
        "like_count": 584,
        "quote_count": 3,
        "reply_count": 5,
        "retweet_count": 94
      },
      "text": "A simple formula for being great at anything:\n\n1) Spend a LOT of time on it. Unreasonable amounts\n2) Find a teacher who instills a love of excellence and a love of craft\n3) Constantly seek the feedback of honest critics\n4) Treat failure as a vehicle for learning\n5) Do NOT give up",
      "url": "https://x.com/alexandr_wang/status/1464687343198105601"
    },
    {
      "author_id": "615818451",
      "created_at": "2021-11-26T19:10:10.000Z",
      "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
        "1464310529204183041"
      ],
      "id": "1464310529204183041",
      "public_metrics": {
        "bookmark_count": 1,
        "impression_count": 0,
        "like_count": 12,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "reply_count": 0,
        "retweet_count": 1
      },
      "text": "Another one…\n\n“Heaven and utopia are buckets in a well: when one goes down the other goes up; when religion declines Communism grows.”",
      "url": "https://x.com/alexandr_wang/status/1464310529204183041"
    },
    {
      "author_id": "615818451",
      "created_at": "2021-11-26T18:56:47.000Z",
      "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
        "1464307160549003265"
      ],
      "id": "1464307160549003265",
      "public_metrics": {
        "bookmark_count": 10,
        "impression_count": 0,
        "like_count": 40,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "reply_count": 4,
        "retweet_count": 2
      },
      "text": "Reading this Black Friday, and stumbled upon this showstopper line:\n\n“Nothing is clearer in history than the adoption by successful rebels of the methods they were accustomed to condemn in the forces they deposed.”\n\nThe Lessons of History by Will &amp; Ariel Durant",
      "url": "https://x.com/alexandr_wang/status/1464307160549003265"
    },
    {
      "author_id": "615818451",
      "created_at": "2021-11-22T17:22:00.000Z",
      "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
        "1462833755995914246"
      ],
      "id": "1462833755995914246",
      "public_metrics": {
        "bookmark_count": 18,
        "impression_count": 0,
        "like_count": 117,
        "quote_count": 1,
        "reply_count": 2,
        "retweet_count": 7
      },
      "text": "A successful hedge fund manager told me:\n\n\"I worry about the good years because we learn less about the business in the good years than the bad years.\"\n\nFraming business as a vehicle for continuous learning is key to long-term success—winning comes from learning from your losses.",
      "url": "https://x.com/alexandr_wang/status/1462833755995914246"
    },
    {
      "author_id": "615818451",
      "created_at": "2021-11-21T18:54:06.000Z",
